.Dd October 22, 2026
.Dt PKG6-POLICY 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkg6-policy
.Nd repository catalog, retirement, snapshot and import policy
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa repo/policy.kdl
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The policy of a pkg6 repository controls retirement (see
.Xr pkg6repo-retire 8 ) ,
the versions that must stay visible, protected historical snapshots, and
which packages
.Nm pkg6repo Cm import-pkg5
leaves out.
It is a KDL document, read from
.Pa policy.kdl
in the repository unless a command is given another file with
.Fl -policy .
Without a policy file, retirement is disabled and nothing is kept, excluded
or protected; catalog/1 includes all non-hidden versions.
.Pp
Every file is validated completely before a command changes anything.
Unknown nodes, invalid regular expressions, exact FMRIs without publisher or
timestamp, and zero or unknown durations are errors.
.Ss FMRI rules
Several nodes take an FMRI rule, which is either an argument or a
.Sy regex
property:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Qq Ar fmri
An exact FMRI with publisher and complete timestamped version, for example
.Ql pkg://openindiana.org/library/foo@1.0,5.11-2020.0.1.0:20200101T000000Z .
.It Sy regex= Ns Qq Ar pattern
A regular expression matched against the full FMRI in that form.
.El
.Ss Nodes
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy catalog Brq Sy max-versions Ar N Brq
Bound catalog/1 independently for each publisher and package stem.
.Ar N
must be a whole number at least 1.
Omitting this node preserves the unbounded catalog.
The window includes the newest
.Ar N
non-hidden versions in pkg5 version order, recursively includes only the newest
version satisfying each versioned
.Sy incorporate
constraint reached from a kept version, and includes all keep-rule matches and
protected snapshot closures.
Only versions actually kept extend incorporation closure.
Obsolete and renamed versions count toward the limit.
Timestamp-less prefix pins can match hundreds of historical republishes of the
same release and branch with different timestamps.
A pkg5 client selects the newest permitted version for install or update, so
ordinary incorporation closure retains only that match.
Distinct pins, keep rules and snapshot protection can still exceed
.Ar N .
Protected snapshots retain their existing closure: all versions allowed by their
incorporations and historical resolution of unpinned requirements, as described
under
.Sy snapshot
below.
Retirement-hidden versions remain excluded.
.Pp
Catalog/1 attributes and signatures describe only this window.
Catalog/2 SQLite shards and the depot browser retain all non-hidden history.
Versions outside the window remain fetchable by exact FMRI and payload hash;
the browser versions tab labels them
.Qq not in pkg5 catalog .
A policy edit takes effect on the next catalog rebuild or publication; it does
not delete manifests or payloads.
Windowed imports use a generation-owned metadata ledger after one full bootstrap.
Changing this policy, keep rules or protected snapshots invalidates the ledger
and causes a full rebuild on the next publication.
Retirement and restore publications also rebuild it.
An explicit rebuild always reads the complete manifest history.
.It Sy retirement Brq ...
Policy-driven retirement.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy enabled Cm true Ns | Ns Cm false
Default
.Cm false .
Disabling pauses policy-driven retirement.
It does not restore hidden versions and never deletes anything.
.It Sy inactivity Qq Ar duration
Time a superseded version must go without a qualifying access, counted from
the latest of its supersession, its last access, its last restore and the
time since which access history is proven complete (see
.Xr pkg6repo-retire 8 ) ,
before it is a candidate.
Default
.Qq 12 months .
.It Sy purge-grace Qq Ar duration
Minimum time a version stays hidden before a future purge may remove it.
Default
.Qq 12 months .
Validated and reported; there is no purge in this release.
.El
.Pp
A
.Ar duration
is a positive whole number and a unit:
.Cm days ,
.Cm weeks ,
.Cm months
(calendar months) or
.Cm years ;
the abbreviations
.Cm d ,
.Cm w ,
.Cm mo
and
.Cm y
are accepted.
.It Sy keep Ar rule
Versions that are never retired, never excluded from an import, and always
included in the pkg5 catalog window unless already retirement-hidden.
Keep rules override
.Sy exclude
rules.
.It Sy keep-file Qq Ar path
Read more keep rules from
.Ar path ,
relative to the policy file.
.It Sy import Brq Sy exclude Ar rule ...
New packages of an import that match an
.Sy exclude
rule, and no
.Sy keep
rule, are not imported.
They are listed in the command output and the import receipt.
If a protected snapshot, a package of the same import or a package already
in the repository needs an excluded package, or whether one does cannot be
checked (a version or dependency that is not a pkg5 version), the import
fails and nothing is imported; the error lists the exact
.Sy keep
entries that would resolve it.
.It Sy snapshot Qo Ar name Qc Oo Sy as-of= Ns Qo Ar time Qc Oc Brq ...
A protected historical snapshot, typically the package set of an
installation image.
It contains:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy fmri Qq Ar fmri
An exact member version; repeatable, at least one.
.It Sy source Oo Sy iso= Ns Qo Ar name Qc Oc Oo Sy sha256= Ns Qo Ar hash Qc Oc Oo Sy note= Ns Qo Ar text Qc Oc
Provenance of the member list.
.El
.Pp
The snapshot protects its closure: the members; every version its
incorporations (and those of protected packages) allow; and for every
.Sy require ,
.Sy require-any ,
.Sy group
or
.Sy conditional
dependency no incorporation pins, the newest satisfying version published
at or before
.Sy as-of
(default: the newest member's timestamp), recursively.
Retiring or excluding a version of the closure is refused, and a hidden
version of the closure is reported until it is restored, so the whole
snapshot stays visible to
.Xr pkg 1
for installation and repair.
Members the repository does not hold are reported as unavailable.
.Sy as-of
is written as
.Ql 20201031T235959Z
or in RFC 3339 form.
.El
.Ss Keep files
Keep files hold only keep rules, in one of three forms chosen by the file
name suffix:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa .kdl
.Sy keep
nodes, as in the policy.
.It Pa .json
An array, or an object with a
.Sy keep
array, of exact FMRI strings or objects with one
.Sy exact
or
.Sy regex
member.
.It other
One rule per line: an exact FMRI,
.Ql exact: Ns Ar fmri
or
.Ql regex: Ns Ar pattern .
Empty lines and lines starting with
.Ql #
are ignored.
.El
.Pp
Retirement plans record a digest of the policy and every keep file; a plan
is not applied after any of them changed.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset 2n
retirement {
    enabled true
    inactivity "12 months"
    purge-grace "12 months"
}
keep regex="^pkg://openindiana.org/consolidation/"
keep-file "keep.txt"
import {
    exclude regex="^pkg://openindiana.org/developer/opensolaris/"
}
snapshot "hipster-2020.10" as-of="20201031T235959Z" {
    source iso="OI-hipster-gui-20201031.iso" sha256="..."
    fmri "pkg://openindiana.org/entire@2020.10,5.11-2020.0.1.0:20201031T010203Z"
}
.Ed
.Sh INTERFACE STABILITY
.Sy Uncommitted
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkg 1 ,
.Xr pkg6repo 1 ,
.Xr pkg6depotd 8 ,
.Xr pkg6repo-retire 8
